window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-93534c607369fe88"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"debug-in-ios-simulator\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"ios\">在 iOS 模拟器中调试</h1> <p>使用 Codex 和 XcodeBuildMCP 操作 iOS 模拟器、收集证据，并反复验证修复效果。</p> <p>使用 Codex 找到合适的 Xcode scheme 和模拟器，启动应用、检查 UI 树、点击、输入和滑动、采集截图与日志；必要时连接 LLDB，将模糊的缺陷报告转化为一个经过验证的小修复。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>只在模拟器中经过特定点击、滚动或表单输入流程后才会出现的 UI 问题。</li> <li>应用崩溃、卡住或导航异常，且 Codex 需要先查看日志、截图、视图层级和调试器回溯再编辑代码的情况。</li> <li>希望 Codex 负责复现、修复和验证整个循环，而不必让人手动逐一点击所有状态的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">build-ios-apps（需联网）</a></td> <td>使用 iOS 调试代理通过 XcodeBuildMCP 构建、启动并检查模拟器中的应用，再采集日志、截图和堆栈跟踪，帮助 Codex 缩小问题范围。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技术栈建议</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>需求</th> <th>建议选择</th> <th>原因</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>模拟器自动化</td> <td><a href=\"https://www.xcodebuildmcp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">XcodeBuildMCP（需联网）</a></td> <td>当前工具支持配置模拟器、构建和启动、UI 状态快照、点击、输入、手势、截图、日志采集和连接调试器。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>代理工作流</td> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build iOS Apps 插件（需联网）</a></td> <td>插件的 iOS 调试代理为 Codex 提供了以模拟器为中心的清晰流程，用于复现问题、收集证据，并在每次改动后验证修复。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>应用可观测性</td> <td><code>Logger</code>、<code>OSLog</code>、LLDB 和模拟器截图</td> <td>Codex 可以通过日志和调试器状态解释故障原因，并保存截图证明修复前后的准确 UI 状态。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>复现、诊断并修复一个模拟器问题</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请使用 Build iOS Apps 插件和 XcodeBuildMCP，直接在模拟器中复现此问题、诊断根本原因，并实施小范围修复。\n\n缺陷报告：\n[Describe the expected behavior, the actual bug, and any known screen or account setup.]（描述预期行为、实际问题，以及已知的页面或账户设置。）\n\n约束：\n- 先检查项目、scheme 和模拟器是否已经选定。如果没有，先找到正确的 Xcode 项目或 workspace，选择应用 scheme 和模拟器，并在本次会话的后续步骤中沿用这套设置。\n- 在模拟器中构建并启动应用。开始交互之前，通过 UI 状态快照或截图确认当前显示的是正确页面。\n- 亲自在模拟器中通过点击、输入、滚动和滑动重现准确的问题路径。优先使用无障碍标签或 ID，而不是裸坐标；布局变化后，在下一步操作前重新读取 UI 层级。\n- 调试时采集证据：记录视觉状态的截图、失败前后的模拟器日志；如果问题像是崩溃或卡住，再采集 LLDB 堆栈帧或变量。\n- 如果模拟器尚未启动，请启动一个并告诉我选用的设备和操作系统。如果需要凭据或专用测试样本，请只针对缺少的输入暂停并询问。\n- 做出能够解决问题的最小代码改动，然后重新运行模拟器流程，并准确说明你如何验证修复。\n\n交付内容：\n- Codex 执行的问题复现步骤\n- 能解释问题的关键截图、日志或堆栈信息\n- 代码修复及其有效原因\n- 最终验证使用的模拟器和 scheme\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build iOS Apps 插件（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">模型上下文协议</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">代理技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"give-codex-the-whole-simulator-loop\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex\">让 Codex 负责完整的模拟器调试循环</h2> <p>最适合让 Codex 负责整个循环：选择正确的应用目标，在模拟器中启动应用、检查当前界面、执行问题复现步骤、收集日志和截图、必要时查看堆栈跟踪、修改代码，然后再次运行同一路径，确认问题已经解决。</p> <p>如果希望整个流程都由代理完成，请使用 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build iOS Apps 插件（需联网）</a>。它的 iOS 调试工作流以 XcodeBuildMCP 为核心，因此 Codex 能与已启动的模拟器交互，并收集通常需要人工手动获取的相同证据。</p> <p>在 XcodeBuildMCP 配置好模拟器自动化、UI 自动化、调试和日志流程后，Codex 就可以负责完整的复现、调试和验证循环。如果 Codex 尚未选择项目、scheme 和模拟器，请先让它发现并选定这些对象，然后在本次会话后续步骤中复用该设置。</p> <p><a id=\"leverage-what-xcodebuildmcp-can-do\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"xcodebuildmcp\">发挥 XcodeBuildMCP 的能力</h2> <p>可以在提示词中让 Codex 使用以下实用能力：</p> <ul> <li><strong>发现项目和模拟器：</strong>检查 Codex 是否已经知道要使用的应用目标和模拟器；查找 Xcode 项目或 workspace、列出 scheme、找到或启动模拟器，并在后续构建和运行步骤中保持设置稳定。</li> <li><strong>控制构建和启动：</strong>构建当前应用目标、在模拟器中安装并启动构建结果；需要时重新启动并采集日志；如果 Codex 需要检查应用运行日志，则解析应用的 bundle ID。</li> <li><strong>检查并操作 UI：</strong>读取屏幕上的无障碍层级、截图、点击控件、在输入框中键入内容、滚动列表，以及执行边缘滑动等模拟器手势。</li> <li><strong>查看日志和调试器状态：</strong>持续读取模拟器日志，将 LLDB 连接到运行中的应用，设置断点，检查堆栈帧和局部变量，并在崩溃或卡住需要深入分析时运行调试器命令。</li> </ul> <p>关键习惯是：先让 Codex 检查视图树，再点击控件。XcodeBuildMCP 会提供无障碍层级及对应坐标，因此 Codex 可以优先使用稳定的标签或元素 ID，而不是猜测屏幕坐标。</p> <p><a id=\"turn-a-vague-bug-into-a-reproducible-script\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">把模糊的缺陷变成可复现的步骤</h2> <p>iOS 调试技能最适合这样的提示词：指出一个具体缺陷和一个明确的预期结果，然后让 Codex 自行操作应用并收集证据。如果需要登录、深层链接或测试样本，请一次说明；只有在缺失输入确实阻碍工作时，才让 Codex 暂停询问。</p> <p><a id=\"practical-tips\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">实用技巧</h2> <p><a id=\"ask-for-evidence-not-just-a-fix\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">要求提供证据，而不只是修复</h3> <p>请 Codex 列出准确的模拟器、scheme、截图、日志片段和用于解释问题的堆栈信息。与“我觉得这样应该能修好”相比，这些内容能让你更容易审查最终补丁。</p> <p><a id=\"prefer-accessibility-labels-over-coordinates\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">优先使用无障碍标签，而不是坐标</h3> <p>如果某个控件没有稳定标签或无障碍标识符，导致 Codex 不得不通过坐标点击，请让它明确指出。这通常说明修复中也可以加入一项小的 UI 可测试性改进。</p> <p><a id=\"keep-one-bug-per-run\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_10\">每次只处理一个缺陷</h3> <p>通过模拟器操作进行调试很有力，但一次只针对一种故障模式的提示词通常更容易验证。先完成一轮复现、修复和验证，再扩展到相邻问题。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"debug-in-ios-simulator\">Debug in iOS simulator</h1> <p>Use Codex and XcodeBuildMCP to drive your app in iOS Simulator, capture evidence, and iterate toward a fix.</p> <p>Use Codex to discover the right Xcode scheme and simulator, launch the app, inspect the UI tree, tap, type, swipe, capture screenshots and logs, attach LLDB when needed, and turn a vague bug report into a small verified fix.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>UI bugs that only show up after a specific tap, scroll, or form entry path in Simulator</li> <li>Crashes, hangs, or broken navigation where Codex needs logs, screenshots, view hierarchy state, and a debugger backtrace before editing code</li> <li>Teams that want Codex to own the reproduce-fix-verify loop instead of asking a human to manually click through every state</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">build-ios-apps (online)</a></td> <td>Use the iOS debugger agent to build, launch, inspect, and drive an app on a simulator with XcodeBuildMCP, then capture logs, screenshots, and stack traces while Codex narrows the bug.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\">Tech stack recommendations</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Need</th> <th>Good default</th> <th>Why</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Simulator automation</td> <td><a href=\"https://www.xcodebuildmcp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">XcodeBuildMCP (online)</a></td> <td>The current tool surface covers simulator setup, build and launch, UI snapshots, taps, typing, gestures, screenshots, log capture, and debugger attachment.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Agent workflow</td> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build iOS Apps plugin (online)</a></td> <td>The plugin's iOS debugger agent gives Codex a clear simulator-first loop for reproducing a bug, gathering evidence, and validating the fix after each change.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>App observability</td> <td><code>Logger</code>, <code>OSLog</code>, LLDB, and Simulator screenshots</td> <td>Codex can use logs and debugger state to explain what broke, then save screenshots to prove the exact UI state before and after the fix.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Reproduce, Diagnose, and Fix One Simulator Bug</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the Build iOS Apps plugin and XcodeBuildMCP to reproduce this bug directly in Simulator, diagnose the root cause, and implement a small fix.\n\nBug report:\n[Describe the expected behavior, the actual bug, and any known screen or account setup.]\n\nConstraints:\n- First check whether a project, scheme, and simulator are already selected. If not, discover the right Xcode project or workspace, pick the app scheme, choose a simulator, and reuse that setup for the rest of the session.\n- Build and launch the app in Simulator, then confirm the right screen is visible with a UI snapshot or screenshot before you start interacting with it.\n- Drive the exact reproduction path yourself by tapping, typing, scrolling, and swiping in the simulator. Prefer accessibility labels or IDs over raw coordinates, and re-read the UI hierarchy before the next action when the layout changes.\n- Capture evidence while you debug: screenshots for visual state, simulator logs around the failure, and LLDB stack frames or variables if the bug looks like a crash or hang.\n- If the simulator is not already booted, boot one and tell me which device and OS you chose. If credentials or a special fixture are required, pause and ask only for that missing input.\n- Make the smallest code change that addresses the bug, then rerun the simulator flow and tell me exactly how you verified the fix.\n\nDeliver:\n- the reproduction steps Codex executed\n- the key screenshots, logs, or stack details that explained the bug\n- the code fix and why it works\n- the simulator and scheme used for final verification\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build iOS Apps plugin (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">Model Context Protocol</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"give-codex-the-whole-simulator-loop\">Give Codex the whole simulator loop</h2> <p>This use case works best when Codex owns the full loop: choose the right app target, launch the app in Simulator, inspect the current screen, perform the reproduction steps, gather logs and screenshots, inspect a stack trace if needed, patch the code, and rerun the same path to prove the bug is gone.</p> <p>Use the <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build iOS Apps plugin (online)</a> when you want that loop to stay agentic. Its iOS debugger workflow is built around XcodeBuildMCP, which means Codex can interact with a booted simulator and gather the same evidence a human would normally collect by hand.</p> <p>When XcodeBuildMCP is configured with simulator automation, UI automation, debugging, and logging workflows, Codex can own the full reproduce-debug-verify loop. If Codex has not picked a project, scheme, and simulator yet, ask it to discover those first and reuse that setup for the rest of the session.</p> <h2 id=\"leverage-what-xcodebuildmcp-can-do\">Leverage what XcodeBuildMCP can do</h2> <p>These are the practical capability groups to prompt Codex to use:</p> <ul> <li>Project and simulator discovery: check whether Codex already knows which app target and simulator to use, discover the Xcode project or workspace, enumerate schemes, find or boot a simulator, and keep that setup stable for future build/run steps.</li> <li>Build and launch control: build the active app target, install and launch the simulator build, relaunch with log capture when needed, and resolve the app bundle id if Codex needs to inspect app-specific runtime logs.</li> <li>UI inspection and interaction: read the on-screen accessibility hierarchy, take screenshots, tap controls, type into fields, scroll through lists, and perform edge swipes or other simulator gestures.</li> <li>Logs and debugger state: stream simulator logs, attach LLDB to the running app, set breakpoints, inspect stack frames and local variables, and run debugger commands when a crash or hang needs deeper inspection.</li> </ul> <p>The key habit is to ask Codex to inspect the view tree before it taps. XcodeBuildMCP exposes the accessibility hierarchy plus coordinates, so Codex can prefer stable labels or element IDs instead of guessing raw screen positions.</p> <h2 id=\"turn-a-vague-bug-into-a-reproducible-script\">Turn a vague bug into a reproducible script</h2> <p>The iOS debugger skill is most effective when your prompt gives one concrete bug and one expected outcome, then lets Codex drive the app and collect evidence autonomously. If a login, deep link, or test fixture is required, say that once and ask Codex to pause only when that missing input blocks progress.</p> <h2 id=\"practical-tips\">Practical tips</h2> <h3 id=\"ask-for-evidence-not-just-a-fix\">Ask for evidence, not just a fix</h3> <p>Request the exact simulator, scheme, screenshots, log snippets, and stack details that Codex used to explain the bug. That makes the final patch much easier to review than \"I think this should fix it.\"</p> <h3 id=\"prefer-accessibility-labels-over-coordinates\">Prefer accessibility labels over coordinates</h3> <p>If Codex has to tap by coordinates because a control has no stable label or accessibility identifier, ask it to call that out. That is often a signal that the bug fix should include a small UI testability improvement too.</p> <h3 id=\"keep-one-bug-per-run\">Keep one bug per run</h3> <p>A simulator-driven debugging loop is powerful, but it is still easier to trust when one prompt targets one failure mode. Ask Codex to finish one reproduce-fix-verify cycle before expanding to adjacent issues.</p>"};
